  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: SQL_ORDER_BY
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: SQL_ORDER_BY
  language: 3
  conceptTitle: 'ORDER BY: Sorting Results'
  symbol: ORDER
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - SQL_03_ORDER_BY
  - HZ_SQL_04_ORDER_BY
  topics:
  - ORDER BY
  definition: ORDER BY sorts the rows of a result by one column.
  howItWorks: Add ORDER BY and a column name at the end of the query. ASC (ascending)
    sorts from smallest to biggest, A to Z, or earliest to latest - it is used when
    you write nothing. DESC (descending) sorts the other way.
  exampleCode: "Table: pets\n id | name  | animal | age\n  1 | Bolt  | Dog    |  
    4\n  2 | Misty | Cat    |   2\n  3 | Rex   | Dog    |   7\n\nSELECT name FROM
    pets\nORDER BY age;"
  exampleExplanation: ORDER BY age sorts by the age column. With no ASC or DESC it
    sorts smallest first, so the result is Misty (2), Bolt (4), Rex (7). Adding DESC
    would reverse the order.
  tip: ORDER BY comes at the end of a query, after WHERE.
